   "user_view_type": "public",
   "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "A periodic recovery checkpoint can sample recovery points before log truncation and write them after the truncation checkpoint. The existing file lock serializes writes but leaves sampling outside the critical section. The resulting stale checkpoint can cause startup recovery to skip an unflushed segment.\r\n\r\nSerialize recovery point sampling and checkpoint writing on the per-directory `OffsetCheckpointFile` instance. Both truncation paths use the same critical section. The checkpoint format is unchanged.\r\n\r\nAdd a parameterized regression test covering `truncateTo` and `truncateFullyAndStartAt`. It coordinates checkpointing with truncation, verifies the persisted recovery point, and then rolls the log, injects CRC corruption into the unflushed earlier segment, and reopens it to verify recovery truncates the damaged data.\r\n\r\nTesting:\r\n- Before the fix, both concurrency cases failed with `expected: <0> but was: <10>`.\r\n- After the fix, all 82 tests in `LogManagerTest` and `LogLoaderTest` passed.\r\n- Storage Checkstyle and SpotBugs checks passed.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n./gradlew :storage:test \\\r\n  --tests 'org.apache.kafka.storage.internals.log.LogManagerTest' \\\r\n  --tests 'org.apache.kafka.storage.internals.log.LogLoaderTest' \\\r\n  -PmaxParallelForks=1 -PmaxTestRetries=0\r\n```",
